## The five tabs

- **Observations** — what staff recorded about your child, usually with photos.
- **Student** — your child's profile.
- **Calendar** — what's coming up.
- **Themes** — the theme plans the setting is working through.
- **Payments** — your payment records.

{% callout type="note" %}
Staff call observations **activities** in their own app. If a teacher refers to "the activity I
added", that's the same thing you see under **Observations**.
{% /callout %}

## Finding a particular observation

Observations filter by **growth milestone**, **activity type** and **date**, with **Clear** to reset
them. The growth-milestone filter is the useful one when you want to see progress in a single area
over time rather than reading the feed day by day.

## Payments

The Payments tab lists your payment records and takes you out to the payment page when something is
due. If it says no payment records were found, the setting hasn't raised anything against your
account — it isn't a sign the app failed to load them.

## More than one child, or more than one parent

Accounts are saved **on the device**, and **Switch account** moves between them without signing out
and back in. **Add another account** adds one to the device.

Two things follow from accounts being device-local:

- A new phone starts with no saved accounts. That's expected — sign in once and it's saved again.
- **Remove account** takes it off *that device only*. The account itself still exists, and you can
  sign back in with it.

